# Docs sync on integration changes

When a change adds a dependency, an environment variable, or edits build / CI / config files, update in the **same** change:

- `README.md` — setup, env, how to run, new limitations
- `.env.example` — every new variable, with a one-line comment
- `AGENTS.md` / `CLAUDE.md` — only if the workflow, the stack line or a hard ban changed
- the relevant domain doc in `docs/` — if a convention in a fragile zone changed

The stop-hook asks for this when an integration-level file was edited. If nothing needs updating, say so explicitly — do not pad docs to satisfy the hook.

Do not create a second "full README" inside rules; rules hold conventions, README holds facts.
